  "patch_sha256": "9b2132391fa6b93b493c0ae909570ab0671e8cb6a30b7bcecc4e4099ae037eb2",
  "base_binding": "Exact current checkout SHA256 per existing path; unrelated process-final callback one-character root correction does not overlap these files. Root source/tree binding required at adoption.",
  "dependency_contract": "Apply ownership with propagation revision as one coherent compile candidate; field changes and handler result types depend on both. No Cargo/dependency changes. Lower service/transport proposal depends on these APIs but is not included.",
  "review_units": {
    "async_utils_primitive": 325,
    "session_prewarm_refresh": 86,
    "connection_shutdown": 78
  },
  "tests": "Five new primitive tests, two refresh gate tests, one connection panic test; existing cancellation test now rejoins and checks exact attached owner. None executed.",
  "limits": [
    "RetainedTask owns an exact Tokio task and original terminal result. It does not retain every resource captured by a runtime-cancelled future; lower resource owners must hold those resources independently.",
    "McpConnectionSet shutdown success means its shutdown task joined; current RmcpClient still drops RunningService without an observed close. No lower transport/process-group or whole-host clean proof.",
    "Unobserved successful and failed tasks remain globally reachable; process-wide aggregate/drain of owners whose manager disappeared is not implemented here.",
    "McpRuntime shutdown here observes current connection snapshot only. Old/replaced and partially constructed lower service generations require the separate lower roster proposal.",
    "Session refresh close waits for the outstanding semaphore permit; arbitrary noncooperative refresh work can exceed an observer deadline.",
    "No new HTTP worker completeness proof; pinned RMCP hides some internal close errors."
  ]
}
